#subtitle: Setting the party's ideological direction.

= Questions of Ideology

The RSDRP(O) is torn between many different ideological currents. What should be our primary ideological guidance for now?

[? if ideology != 0 : We have previously chosen a [+ ideology +] ideology. Changing it will likely have drawbacks. ?]

- @class_struggle: Class struggle and preparing the proletariat for the revolution are our primary goals.
- @centrist: The Center Marxism of Karl Kautsky and Menshevism of Yuliy Martov remains the best way to resolve our internal contradictions.
- @labor: We should work with the trade unions and soviets to improve the lives of workers immediately, focusing on real, tangible results.
- @reform: Following the Liquidationists, we should work for ethical socialism, strengthen democracy, and expand the party's electorate.
- @marxghost: Using the power of Enlightened Centrism, Kautskyism, and the sheer willpower of the few remaining in our party, Martov summons the Spirit of Karl Marx himself to save Russian Socialism.
- @easy_discard

@class_struggle
choose-if: rsrpi_formed = 0
unavailable-subtitle: The Party Left has split.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.ideology && Q.ideology != "left") {
    Q.changed = 1;
}
!}
go-to: changed if changed = 1
on-departure: ideology = "left"; left_strength += 10; communist_coalition += 1; left_dissent -= 5; z_relation -= 3; kadets_relation -= 5; nationalization_support += 1; rkp_relation += 3

The radical left of the party supports a course of class struggle, and potentially a reconcilliation with the Far-Left.

@centrist
choose-if: centrists_resign = 0
unavailable-subtitle: The Party Center has split.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.ideology && Q.ideology != "centrist") {
    Q.changed = 1;
}
!}
go-to: changed if changed = 1
on-departure: ideology = "centrist"; center_strength += 10; center_dissent -= 10; left_dissent -= 5; reformist_dissent -= 5

The Center Marxists, represented by Martov and Axelrod, support a middle course of preparing for revolution while building up the consciousness of the working class.

@labor
choose-if: unions_independent = 0
unavailable-subtitle: The Unions have split.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.ideology && Q.ideology != "labor") {
    Q.changed = 1;
}
!}
go-to: changed if changed = 1
on-departure: ideology = "labor"; labor_strength += 10; wtb_support += 1; labor_dissent -= 5; rkp_relation -= 3

The labor wing of the party supports continued particpation in government in order to provide benefits to the workers, and the creation of public works programs for employment.

@reform
unavailable-subtitle: The Party Right has split.
choose-if: reformists_resign = 0
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.ideology && Q.ideology != "reformist") {
    Q.changed = 1;
}
!}
go-to: changed if changed = 1
on-departure: ideology = "reformist"; reformist_strength += 10; democratization += 1; reformist_dissent -= 5; z_relation += 5; kadets_relation += 5; rkp_relation -= 8; moderate_plan_support += 1

The Liquidationist wing of the party seeks to preserve the Republic and the democratic system of government, and is most supportive of coalitions with the other pro-democracy parties.

@marxghost
subtitle: Using the power of Enlightened Centrism, Kautskyism, and the sheer willpower of the few remaining in our party, Martov summons the Spirit of Karl Marx himself to save Russian Socialism.
view-if: reformists_resign = 1 and unions_independent = 1 and centrists_resign = 1 and left_split = 1
on-arrival: ideology = "partydeath"

@changed
on-arrival: left_dissent += 5; center_dissent += 5; labor_dissent += 5; reformist_dissent += 5

We have changed ideologies. Many in the party feel unmoored.
